  "roles_note": "start_role mission: taps release at max(release[p], S + release[p]); start_role bootstrap: taps (and core resets with role bootstrap) release at release[p] (raw delivered wavefront, boot runs before START), the local START tap start_t<start_tap> at S + release[p] gates the contents' declared mission admission.  One START, no timer, no die-reset bypass.",
  "note": "OWNER DECISION 13c: START rides the reset wavefront (start_i / start_o_<k> beside arst_n / rst_o_<k>, run relays on the reset relay sites).  Soft partition p's control state (leaves, boundary epochs, hard-core resets) releases at  max(release[p], S + release[p])  clocks, S = the die start pin's rising edge relative to rst_n deassert; i.e. the START offsets ARE the published release offsets.  Hard partitions (prebuilt, no start pin) see the raw reset only."
